ies because  look you've got migrants that are taking  their life  and putting it at risk their and their  children's they've got to pay these uh  these smugglers  these traffickers thousands of dollars  you know customers of border patrol  they they estimated that those smugglers  that those uh cartels  made at least 400 million dollars last  month alone  uh smuggling you know uh migrants into  into this country and so it is a  humanitarian problem  we need to disincentivize this surge we  need to tell people hey  you know don't come to the united states  we're going to abide by our laws i think  one of the things we need to do ada  had a heck of a lot more judges so that  a lot of these  asylum cases can be done quickly uh have  them stay in  in mexico not you know we we had an  agreement with them they would stay in  mexico  that was broken we had agreements with  the central american countries  that was broken all that incentivized  all this this  surge that we have we're seeing right  now and by the way it's only going to  get worse  this is just the beginning of this tidal  wave that's going to come our way  representative jimenez thank you very  much
 

